e, keeping the size manageable at 330 lines. I\u2019ll start by changing the import block to include `flutter/foundation.dart`. I\u2019ll ensure I match the `oldText` snippets exactly when doing that. Then, I\u2019ll modify the constructor signature.\n\n**Updating constructor and fields**\n\nI\u2019m looking at the current constructor for `HeroFeedbackSurface` and need to add new fields for `onSeekPreview`, `onSeekDragStarted`, and `onSeekDragEnded`. It makes sense to place these before the vertical drag parameters to keep the order neat. \n\nI\u2019ll also insert new callback fields in the class fields section, using `final VoidCallback? onSeekDragStarted;`, `final VoidCallback? onSeekDragEnded;`, and `final void Function(int targetMs, int durationMs)? onSeekPreview;`. It's a good idea to ensure we import whatever we need from foundation. I\u2019ll also add a static key for UI tests after `seekHudKey`. Finally, within the build method, I\u2019ll implement the calls for `onSeekDragStarted` and `onSeekPreview` after defining `onSeekStart`.\n\n**Modifying seek callbacks**\n\nCurrently, I have a method `onSeekStart` that I need to modify to call `onSeekDragStarted` and `onSeekPreview`. Before calling `onSeekPreview`, I'll ensure to set the `seekTargetMs.value` and confirm `seeking.value = true`. \n\nIn `onSeekUpdate`, I\u2019ll call `onSeekPreview` with the updated value of `seekTargetMs` to avoid excessive calls. For `onSeekEnd`, I\u2019ll store duration and target, then call `onSeekDragEnded` and finally the `onSeek` method. I want the ended callback to manage temporary feedback without affecting the seek commit, so I\u2019ll place it before the commit. Lastly, I\u2019ll update the center seek HUD condition and define `showCenterSeekHud` appropriately.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_049c12b31822c5ba016a881142aeb881949b378fc28a513cc7\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"content\":[],\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABqiBFpjPDbODcVs8X8atXBagCRc5oLMfYqKWkPcQrJXNAv1Rpx0cWufUzTNWoo